section.center#firstslide(data-transition="fade", data-state="hide-menubar")
	h1 Simplemenu
	h3 for Reveal.js
	p.smaller Manual menu, linking to #[code id]

section#firstmenuitem.center
	h4 Why?
	p Sometimes manually linking the menu is needed. Simplemenu can do that too.
	p.small Manually linking can be done through #[code id] and #[code data-name]. #[br]These slides explain the use of #[code id].

section#secondmenuitem.center
	section
		h4 It's easy to set up, but expects a few things:
		ul.small
			li Menu items can only be top-level sections: regular horizontal slides or vertical stacks.
			li Create an element that will hold the links. 
			li Inside this main menu, there have to be anchors with an href.
			li These need to point to an ID of a regular slide, a stack or the first slide in a stack.

	section
		h4 JavaScript
		p.small Load the Simplemenu script and make a reference to it in the Reveal plugin options.
		br
		pre
				code.hljs.html(data-line-numbers).
					&lt;script src="plugin/simplemenu/simplemenu.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
					&lt;script&gt;
						Reveal.initialize({
							plugins: [ Simplemenu ]
						});
					&lt;script&gt;
	section
		h4 HTML Markup
		p.small Make anchors in your links to the ID's of your sections. Use the #[code #/anchor] notation that Reveal uses.
		pre
			code.hljs.html(data-line-numbers).
				&lt;nav class="menubar"&gt;
				    &lt;ul class="menu"&gt;
				        &lt;li&gt;
				            &lt;a href="#/firstmenuitem"&gt;First menu item&lt;/a&gt;
				        &lt;/li&gt;
				    &lt;/ul&gt;
				&lt;/nav&gt;
				&lt;div class="slides"&gt;
				    &lt;section id="firstmenuitem"&gt;
				        //...
				    &lt;/section&gt;
				        //...
				&lt;/div&gt;
	section
		h4 That’s it!